 "about_text": "Yutaka Kikutake Gallery opened in Roppongi, Tokyo, in 2015, later adding a second space in Kyobashi in 2024. The gallery presents exhibitions of international and domestic artists, supporting their practices and seeking opportunities to present their work internationally. Grounded in a strong sense of recent art history, the program explores newly created forms of expression and emphasizes art's contribution to society. Beyond exhibitions, the gallery runs workshops for all ages and publishes artist books alongside the lifestyle and culture magazine Chic and the art criticism journal Kyoku. The Kyobashi space focuses on group exhibitions reflecting the gallery's core values.",
